```java
// ═══ INHERITANCE: exposes EVERYTHING from parent ═══
public class Account {
    public void deposit(BigDecimal amount) { ... }
    public void withdraw(BigDecimal amount) { ... }
    public void transferInternational(String country, BigDecimal amount) { ... }
    public void closeAccount() { ... }
}

public class SavingsAccount extends Account {
    // INHERITS ALL: deposit, withdraw, transferInternational, closeAccount
    // transferInternational() is UNWANTED for savings — but it's inherited and PUBLIC!
    // Caller: savingsAccount.transferInternational("USA", 50000) ← SHOULDN'T be allowed!
}

// ═══ DELEGATION: forwards ONLY what you choose ═══
public class SavingsAccountService {
    private final Account delegate;  // HAS-A — holds delegate

    public SavingsAccountService(Account delegate) {
        this.delegate = delegate;
    }

    // FORWARD: deposit — with extra validation
    public void deposit(BigDecimal amount) {
        if (amount.compareTo(new BigDecimal("10000000")) > 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Savings deposit limit: Rs.1 crore");
        }
        delegate.deposit(amount);  // DELEGATE the actual work
    }

    // FORWARD: withdraw — with minimum balance check
    public void withdraw(BigDecimal amount) {
        delegate.withdraw(amount);  // DELEGATE
    }

    // NOT FORWARDED: transferInternational — deliberately HIDDEN!
    // closeAccount — deliberately HIDDEN!
    // Caller CANNOT call savingsService.transferInternational() — method doesn't exist!
}
```

Three benefits of delegation over inheritance:

```java
// BENEFIT 1: CONTROL — expose only what makes sense
// Inheritance: ALL parent methods visible. Can't hide transferInternational().
// Delegation: forward deposit + withdraw. Hide everything else.

// BENEFIT 2: ADD LOGIC — decorate before/after delegation
public void deposit(BigDecimal amount) {
    log.info("Before deposit: {}", amount);     // BEFORE
    validate(amount);                            // ADDED validation
    delegate.deposit(amount);                    // DELEGATE
    notifyCustomer("Deposited Rs." + amount);    // AFTER
}
// With inheritance: adding logic requires overriding + super.deposit() — fragile.

// BENEFIT 3: SWAP — change delegate at runtime
public class FlexibleService {
    private AccountOperations delegate;

    public void setDelegate(AccountOperations newDelegate) {
        this.delegate = newDelegate;  // SWAP at runtime!
    }
}
// Production: new FlexibleService(new PostgresAccountOps())
// Testing: new FlexibleService(new MockAccountOps())
// Inheritance: parent fixed at compile time — can't swap.
```

